  uid=g3:1_64 main
    uid=g3:1_65 StaticText "AGORA / FIELD GUIDE"
    uid=g3:1_66 heading "Local room" level="1"
    uid=g3:1_67 heading "What it is" level="2"
    uid=g3:1_68 StaticText "The local-development room is the first place a person types into Agora: one project, one room, on this machine, over loopback, opted into explicitly. Its delivery is split into five slices. This candidate covers L1/L2 implementation plus independently testable L5 preparation. It is stacked on the unlanded L2 candidate, not a completed usable room. L1 published the conversation contracts, one JSON Schema 2020-12 family in "
    uid=g3:1_69 link "local-room.schema.json" url="http://127.0.0.1:4178/source/contracts/schemas/local-room.schema.json.html"
      uid=g3:1_70 StaticText "local-room.schema.json"
    uid=g3:1_71 StaticText " with ten closed components. L2 makes the room durable: a send is committed to PostgreSQL in one transaction, and the room reads back in the same order after the service restarts. Cursors and the base receipt reuse the "
    uid=g3:1_72 link "synchronization values" url="http://127.0.0.1:4178/source/contracts/schemas/sync.schema.json.html"
      uid=g3:1_73 StaticText "synchronization values"
    uid=g3:1_74 StaticText "; errors reuse the "
    uid=g3:1_75 link "stable reason codes" url="http://127.0.0.1:4178/source/contracts/schemas/errors.schema.json.html"
      uid=g3:1_76 StaticText "stable reason codes"
    uid=g3:1_77 StaticText ", which now include "
    uid=g3:1_78 StaticText "command_conflict"
    uid=g3:1_79 StaticText "."
    uid=g3:1_80 heading "What it does" level="2"
    uid=g3:1_81 StaticText "POST /api/v1/local-room/messages"
    uid=g3:1_82 StaticText " takes a command that names the fixed room, a "
    uid=g3:1_83 StaticText "command_id"
    uid=g3:1_84 StaticText ", a body of 1 to 4096 Unicode scalars and up to ten citations to messages already in the room. The service derives the author; a command never carries one. An accepted command answers 201 with a receipt: the command identity (the id plus the canonical digest of the command bytes), the room revision the message received, the message id and whether the command was replayed. "
    uid=g3:1_85 StaticText "GET /api/v1/local-room/snapshot"
    uid=g3:1_86 StaticText " answers the room's messages in ascending "
    uid=g3:1_87 StaticText "room_seq"
    uid=g3:1_88 StaticText " with the cursor a later subscription must start after, at most the latest 1000 messages."
    uid=g3:1_89 StaticText "Sending the same command again returns the original receipt with "
    uid=g3:1_90 StaticText "replayed: true"
    uid=g3:1_91 StaticText " and stores nothing. Sending the same "
    uid=g3:1_92 StaticText "command_id"
    uid=g3:1_93 StaticText " with a different body is a 409 "
    uid=g3:1_94 StaticText "command_conflict"
    uid=g3:1_95 StaticText ". A command for another project or room is a 404 "
    uid=g3:1_96 StaticText "scope_mismatch"
    uid=g3:1_97 StaticText ". A citation that names no persisted message at its sequence is a 404 "
    uid=g3:1_98 StaticText "not_found"
    uid=g3:1_99 StaticText ". A malformed command is a 400 that names the offending path, and it reaches no storage. Messages, events and receipts are immutable once committed: neither the service role nor the schema owner can update or delete them."
    uid=g3:1_100 heading "Read-only local answer preparation" level="3"
    uid=g3:1_101 StaticText "A separate pure core can prepare an attributed quotation of explicitly selected stored messages. Its visible label is "
    uid=g3:1_102 StaticText "Deterministic local fixture (not AI inference)"
    uid=g3:1_103 StaticText ". Each claim is only that the cited record contains the quoted text, not that its contents are true. It neither answers arbitrary questions nor follows instructions inside messages. Embedded citations and links stay data and never expand the selection."
    uid=g3:1_104 StaticText "This is a contributor-testable package capability, not an Ask center button, a product CLI trigger, or a posted response. Nothing new appears in the room. Posting, cross-restart duplicate suppression and browser visibility remain later L5 work after L3/L4."
    uid=g3:1_105 heading "Why it exists" level="2"
    uid=g3:1_106 StaticText "A room that loses or reorders messages when the process restarts is not a room. Persistence is the first product behavior a person can feel, and it decides the shape of everything after it: the browser room (L4) will render exactly the snapshot this slice returns, and the bounded local answer (L5) will cite exactly the record ids it stores."
    uid=g3:1_107 StaticText "Transactionality is what makes the order trustworthy. The room counter, the message, its "
    uid=g3:1_108 StaticText "message_created"
    uid=g3:1_109 StaticText " event and the command receipt are written in one PostgreSQL transaction. If any of them fails, none of them exists and the counter has not moved, so a rollback never leaves a gap that a later reader would take for a lost message. Concurrent sends serialize on the room's counter row, which is why eight simultaneous commands receive eight contiguous sequences and the event sequence always equals the message sequence. The idempotency identity is the R07 one: the same actor, "
    uid=g3:1_110 StaticText "command_id"
    uid=g3:1_111 StaticText " and request digest replay; a changed digest is refused rather than silently creating a second message. That is what lets a client retry a send after a lost response without fear."
    uid=g3:1_112 heading "How it works" level="2"
    uid=g3:1_113 StaticText "HOW IT WORKS · READ IN ORDER"
    uid=g3:1_114 StaticText "Validate"
    uid=g3:1_115 StaticText "The center runs the shared wire validator; a malformed command is 400 with its path and never reaches the domain or the database."
    uid=g3:1_116 StaticText "Convert and digest"
    uid=g3:1_117 StaticText "Wire values become branded domain values and the request digest is computed over the validated command bytes."
    uid=g3:1_118 StaticText "Open one transaction"
    uid=g3:1_119 StaticText "The adapter binds the fixed project for row-level security and locks the room's counter row; every later step in this request holds that lock."
    uid=g3:1_120 StaticText "Decide"
    uid=g3:1_121 StaticText "The domain replays a matching receipt, denies a changed digest with command_conflict, denies a citation that names no persisted record with not_found, or allocates the next room sequence."
    uid=g3:1_122 StaticText "Append together"
    uid=g3:1_123 StaticText "The message, its message_created event with the same sequence, and the receipt are inserted; commit makes all of them visible at once, rollback none."
    uid=g3:1_124 StaticText "Answer and read back"
    uid=g3:1_125 StaticText "The receipt is answered as 201; a snapshot reads the counter and the messages in one repeatable read, so the cursor and the rows agree even during concurrent sends."
    uid=g3:1_126 StaticText "The pieces stay separable. "
    uid=g3:1_127 link "port.ts" url="http://127.0.0.1:4178/source/packages/domain/src/local-room/port.ts.html"
      uid=g3:1_128 StaticText "port.ts"
    uid=g3:1_129 StaticText " owns the dispatch port, the store port and the send decision; it knows nothing about SQL or HTTP. "
    uid=g3:1_130 link "events.ts" url="http://127.0.0.1:4178/source/packages/domain/src/local-room/events.ts.html"
      uid=g3:1_131 StaticText "events.ts"
    uid=g3:1_132 StaticText " owns the one event kind. "
    uid=g3:1_133 link "local-room.ts" url="http://127.0.0.1:4178/source/packages/storage/src/local-room.ts.html"
      uid=g3:1_134 StaticText "local-room.ts"
    uid=g3:1_135 StaticText " binds the store to one PostgreSQL transaction confined to one project. "
    uid=g3:1_136 link "app.ts" url="http://127.0.0.1:4178/source/apps/center/src/app.ts.html"
      uid=g3:1_137 StaticText "app.ts"
    uid=g3:1_138 StaticText " maps wire to domain and denials to R07 statuses; "
    uid=g3:1_139 link "main.ts" url="http://127.0.0.1:4178/source/apps/center/src/main.ts.html"
      uid=g3:1_140 StaticText "main.ts"
    uid=g3:1_141 StaticText " is the one place the PostgreSQL adapter is composed. A process without that adapter still answers a typed 404 "
    uid=g3:1_142 StaticText "unavailable_capability"
    uid=g3:1_143 StaticText "."
    uid=g3:1_144 StaticText "Storage runs as the non-owner service role. Migration "
    uid=g3:1_145 link "0001_local_room.sql" url="http://127.0.0.1:4178/source/packages/storage/drizzle/0001_local_room.sql.html"
      uid=g3:1_146 StaticText "0001_local_room.sql"
    uid=g3:1_147 StaticText " creates the "
    uid=g3:1_148 StaticText "local_room"
    uid=g3:1_149 StaticText " schema, seeds the one fixed room, forces row-level security keyed on the project, grants the service role only what the path needs (select and the counter column update on the room; select and insert on the three record tables) and adds triggers that refuse updates and deletes for every role, the owner included. The event table's primary key references the message's sequence, so an event cannot exist at a sequence its message does not hold."
    uid=g3:1_150 heading "Selected messages to a cited proposal" level="3"
    uid=g3:1_151 StaticText "HOW IT WORKS · READ IN ORDER"
    uid=g3:1_152 StaticText "Selected messages"
    uid=g3:1_153 StaticText "A trusted caller supplies validated persisted records and an explicit list of stored message IDs from one project and room; no storage handle enters the core."
    uid=g3:1_154 StaticText "Bounded context"
    uid=g3:1_155 StaticText "Refuse more than 100 supplied records, more than 10 selected IDs, or more than 4096 selected body scalars. Sort numerically by room sequence, never timestamp; freeze a private copy and digest it."
    uid=g3:1_156 StaticText "Deterministic proposal"
    uid=g3:1_157 StaticText "Emit exact quotes with the not-AI label. Bind the requester, project, room, request ID and selected content to deterministic identities, with no provider or execution authority."
    uid=g3:1_158 StaticText "Cited records"
    uid=g3:1_159 StaticText "Every claim names its selected stored message ID and exact sequence. Unknown, foreign or unselected citations deny; there is no transitive citation lookup or generated URL."
    uid=g3:1_160 StaticText "Posting boundary"
    uid=g3:1_161 StaticText "A separate type describes a future adapter. No instance exists, no function receives it, and no message is posted."
    uid=g3:1_162 StaticText "The "
    uid=g3:1_163 link "context compiler" url="http://127.0.0.1:4178/source/packages/domain/src/local-answer/context.ts.html"
      uid=g3:1_164 StaticText "context compiler"
    uid=g3:1_165 StaticText ", "
    uid=g3:1_166 link "citation constructor" url="http://127.0.0.1:4178/source/packages/domain/src/local-answer/citations.ts.html"
      uid=g3:1_167 StaticText "citation constructor"
    uid=g3:1_168 StaticText ", "
    uid=g3:1_169 link "proposal function" url="http://127.0.0.1:4178/source/packages/domain/src/local-answer/proposal.ts.html"
      uid=g3:1_170 StaticText "proposal function"
    uid=g3:1_171 StaticText " and "
    uid=g3:1_172 link "future posting port" url="http://127.0.0.1:4178/source/packages/domain/src/local-answer/posting.ts.html"
      uid=g3:1_173 StaticText "future posting port"
    uid=g3:1_174 StaticText " are separate files. They use existing domain values, not new wire contracts. The "
    uid=g3:1_175 link "developer guide" url="http://127.0.0.1:4178/source/docs/runbooks/development.md.html"
      uid=g3:1_176 StaticText "developer guide"
